Package: graphlearnR
Title: Graph Machine Learning and Geometric Deep Learning in R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Adam R", "Sophie", email = "adamrsophie@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: A native R framework for machine learning on graphs, built on
    the 'torch' package without a Python dependency. Provides validated
    graph data structures with explicit one based indexing and edge
    direction semantics, conversion from 'igraph', edge lists and sparse
    matrices, mini-batching of many graphs, vectorized scatter aggregation
    and a general message passing interface, graph neural network layers
    (GraphSAGE, GCN, GIN and GINE, GAT, GATv2, graph transformer
    convolution, edge conditioned convolution, relational GCN), global and
    hierarchical pooling, multi-hop neighbor sampling, leakage safe node,
    edge, graph, group, scaffold and temporal splits, negative sampling,
    heterogeneous graphs with typed relations and typed sampling, temporal
    event graphs, snapshot sequences and spatiotemporal signals with
    recurrent graph models, Graphormer style graph transformers with
    structural encodings, a training loop for node, edge, link and graph
    level tasks, evaluation metrics and post hoc explanations. Layer
    designs follow 'PyTorch Geometric' (Fey and Lenssen 2019)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1903.02428>.
